TI  - Phage biocontrol for reducing bacterial foodborne pathogens in produce and other foods.
AB  - Foodborne pathogen contamination causes approximately 47 million cases of foodborne illness in the United States and renders thousands of pounds of food products inedible, aggravating the already dire situation of food loss. Reducing foodborne contamination not only improves overall global public health but also reduces food waste and loss. Phage biocontrol or phage-mediated reduction of bacterial foodborne pathogens in various foods has been gaining interest recently as an effective and environmentally friendly food-safety approach. Consequently, several commercial phage-based food-safety products have been developed and are increasingly implemented by the food industry in the United States. This review focuses on the use of phage biocontrol in mitigating bacterial pathogen contamination in various food products with a special emphasis on applications to fresh produce.
